# @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone — the DECLARATIVE HALF
# of the kintsugi-on-Rust first lift. Substrate-pull-correct property
# that asserts: across kintsugi ticks, a shard's dark_count is
# monotonic-non-increasing.
#
# Tick 41 / first ouroboros bite. The substrate's first lift of a
# Rust regression test (`bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_ci.rs::dark_count_
# monotone_non_increasing`) into the property+fracture bilateral
# pattern (#53 third instance). Per Taut's substrate-decl response
# to Alex's circular-reflexive Tomm-probe 2026-06-19 evening.
#
# === The recognition (bilateral pattern #53; third instance) ===
#
# First instance: keyword/depth (`5e68df9` property + `d908798`
# fracture) at 2026-06-10.
# Second instance: forward-promised @mirror/fracture/predicate (#272).
# Third instance (THIS): dark_count_monotone.
#
# The pattern's signature: declarative property at
# @epistemologic/property/<predicate> + operational fracture body at
# @kintsugi/fracture/<predicate> via the kintsugi loop bridge. The
# auto-formatting floor.
#
# === The predicate ===
#
# Per @mirror/bench's three-conjunct monotone_non_increasing (the
# substrate-mathematical floor for eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ extended to op-runtime):
# at the dark_count-altitude, the three-conjunct collapses to a
# single-conjunct because:
#
#   - runtime conjunct: not applicable at compile-loss altitude
#                       (compile-loss IS the runtime here)
#   - output conjunct: implicit (the shard's content is stable
#                      across kintsugi-tick if dark_count is the
#                      observable)
#   - env conjunct: implicit (kintsugi ticks happen in the same
#                   substrate environment)
#
# So the predicate reduces to:
#
#   dark_count_monotone(shard, n, np1) ⇔
#     dark_count(shard, np1) ≤ dark_count(shard, n)
#
# This IS the eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ invariant at the substrate-self-hosting
# trajectory altitude. Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s proof: the
# substrate learns from its errors; the errors get smaller; growth is
# monotonically non-decreasing.
#
# === The kintsugi-on-Rust lift trajectory ===
#
# `bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_ci.rs::dark_count_monotone_non_increasing`
# asserts the SAME invariant in Rust. This property lifts the
# assertion to substrate-decl altitude. After the bilateral pair lands
# (this property + fracture body next tick), the Rust test becomes a
# thin shim that calls `mirror verify
# @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone`. The Rust shim itself
# deletes when `mirror.spec` covers it. The ouroboros has bitten.
#
# === Why this lift is safe (Taut's analysis) ===
#
# Today's 38-min pre-push hang did NOT regress dark_count — it
# regressed compile-time. The lift demonstrates the bilateral pattern
# without breaking; primes the next lift
# (cold_compile_within_tolerance) which WOULD have caught today.
#
# === Composes with @mirror/bench ===
#
# This property's verdict feeds @mirror/bench's regress_check via
# composition. When kintsugi runs at tick n+1, the bench crystal for
# the shard's dark_count carries the measurement; the property's
# verdict gates whether the substrate-pull is admissible. Same shape
# as the @magic/audit ⇔ contract.invariant_preserved pair at the
# verifier altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   monotone invariants        Floyd-Hoare-Dijkstra; the classical
#                              loop-invariant discipline. This
#                              property IS that invariant at the
#                              substrate-pull-loop altitude.
#   property-based testing     QuickCheck (Claessen-Hughes 2000);
#                              shrinking-counterexamples for monotone
#                              predicates. The bilateral fracture
#                              body emits the shrunk repair.
#   ranking functions          termination proofs via well-founded
#                              orders; dark_count is the ranking
#                              function for substrate-pull progress.
#
# Spec context: shards/mirror/bench.mirror (the @mirror/bench
#               substrate-decl this property composes); recognition
#               #87 candidate (the ouroboros bites).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       this property is the first ouroboros bite),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53 pattern; this is the third instance),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (shard and tick are
#                       typed carriers).
# Related shards: mirror/bench.mirror (the bench substrate-decl this
#                  property composes via monotone_non_increasing),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (the loop-discipline family this
#                  property runs at; tick is from
#                  @epistemologic/reality/time inherited via
#                  @kintsugi),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (the OPERATIONAL HALF of this bilateral pair;
#                  forward-promised in this same tick).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/programming/claessen-hughes-2000

# === The shard carrier ===
#
# Typed reference to the substrate-decl shard being checked. Forward-
# promised refinement: typed parametric shard once the substrate's
# shard type lands at @mirror/store altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type shard = ref

# === The tick carrier ===
#
# Typed reference to a kintsugi tick. Forward-promised refinement:
# inherits from @epistemologic/reality/time once that family lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type tick = ref

# === dark_count_monotone predicate (the declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that the shard's
# dark_count at tick n+1 is bounded above by dark_count at tick n.
# Per the substrate's eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ proof from boot/00-prism.mirror.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the @kintsugi loop's
# active_pass reads this predicate when verifying substrate-pull
# progress. The operational half (the fracture body that emits a
# repair morphism when this predicate fails) lives at
# @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone (forward-promised in this
# same tick).
#
# Bounded → substrate-pull is honest (dark_count is non-increasing).
# Unbounded → substrate-pull regressed at tick n+1 (the kintsugi loop
# must re-converge before further ticks are admissible).
dark_count_monotone(shard: shard, n: tick, np1: tick) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone
out shard
out tick
out dark_count_monotone
